{{Short description|Chronology of the board game Go}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=November 2026}}

[[File:MET DP135836.jpg|thumb|right|upright=1.3|''Outfit for the Go Game'', woodblock print (''surimono''), 19th century, [[Metropolitan Museum of Art]].]]
This is a timeline of the history of the board game [[Go (game)|Go]] (Chinese ''weiqi'', Korean ''baduk''), from its legendary origins in ancient China to the age of AI. For the full story, see [[History of Go]].
